---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Badge from '../components/ui/Badge.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const lastUpdated = 'March 15, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use // OTHR Creative Engineering"
  description="Commercial engagement terms, intellectual property rights, and terms of service for OTHR Engineering Studio."
>
  <div class="py-16 md:py-24 border-b border-[#E2DDD1] bg-[#F5F2EB]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-body text-xs text-neutral-500 mb-6">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#0D111C] transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[#0232d4] font-semibold">Terms</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <Badge variant="primary">Studio Terms</Badge>
        <span class="text-xs text-neutral-500 font-medium">Effective: {lastUpdated}</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="font-display font-extrabold text-4xl sm:text-6xl text-[#0D111C] mb-6">
        Terms of Use<span class="text-[#0232d4]">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="font-body text-lg text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">
        The guidelines governing your use of this digital platform, open-source code demonstrations, and engagement with OTHR Engineering Studio.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-16 bg-[#F5F2EB]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12 font-body text-base text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[#0D111C]">01. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing this website, reading our engineering journal, or submitting a project inquiry, you agree to comply with these terms of use. If you do not agree, please discontinue access.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[#0D111C]">02. Intellectual Property & Code Rights</h2>
        <p>
          Unless otherwise explicitly noted:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-neutral-700">
          <li>All custom visual assets, brand identity elements, and 3D procedural geometries are the proprietary intellectual property of OTHR Engineering Studio.</li>
          <li>Educational code snippets and shader examples provided in The Journal may be referenced under standard permissive fair-use principles with proper attribution.</li>
          <li>Original digital assets, software products, and prototypes created by OTHR remain the intellectual property of OTHR or their respective commissioning organizations.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[#0D111C]">03. Commercial Engagements</h2>
        <p>
          Indicative pricing ranges displayed on the Services page are non-binding estimates intended to assist with budget scoping.
        </p>
        <p>
          A binding commercial commitment is only established upon mutual execution of a formal Statement of Work (SOW) or Master Services Agreement (MSA) signed by both parties.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[#0D111C]">04. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          The website and its interactive code experiments are provided on an "as-is" and "as-available" basis without warranties of any kind. OTHR is not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages resulting from website access or downtime.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
